  // "K38", which was a stronger statement than the evidence supports: "K38" is a marking several makers
  // use, and the model holds exactly one BSS138 row, so there is no second candidate row to constrain
  // the pair to and PartConstrainedToRows would have been a claim dressed up as a bet. The positions
  // stay listed -- NVIDIA's design has them -- with no population claim. What would settle it is on the
  // observation that raised it, where observations live: product.p4261.e1_b's e1_k38_candidate carries
  // the discriminator, "the maker's date-code line, or another maker's marking table, read against
  // Diodes Incorporated's BSS138 table". A second maker's cited row is what would let a claim return.
